; Fail loud on an unsupported Node instead of npm's default warn-only
; EBADENGINE. See docs/adr and issue #420/#410: without this, `npm ci`
; only prints a warning on Node 20 and installs anyway, and the first
; real signal a developer gets is an unrelated-looking vitest/undici
; worker crash deep inside `npm test`.
engine-strict=true
